<title>NETHERLANDS: Grontmij in Polish environment project.</title>
<headline>Grontmij in Polish environment project.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch engineering consultancy Grontmij NV said on Wednesday it had won an order to conduct a feasibility study for a project to clean up industrial waste near the Polish city of Poznan.</p>
<p>A Grontmij spokesman said the study contract was worth several hundreds of thousands of dollars. If it goes ahead, the total project would require an investment of about $30 million.</p>
<p>Grontmij is one of the companies which is currently visiting Poland in a trade mission led by Dutch junior minister of economic affairs Anneke van Dok.</p>
